commit 96fc4e06
author: ViceEye
date: 2026-10-22 17:15:32 -0600
subject: feat(kiro): flatten top-level tool schema combinators + degrade oversized payloads

Port two request-side hardening behaviors from cpa-kiro-provider (ViceEye,
AGPL, self-authored) that upstream Kiro requires:

- normalizeRootSchema: consume top-level allOf/anyOf/oneOf, merge branch
  properties (first writer wins), and drop required entries that reference
  properties absent after the merge. Nested combinators are preserved.
  Also strip $schema/$id/examples/default/title at every level.
- shrinkKiroPayload (wired via KiroExecutor.transformRequest): when the
  serialized payload exceeds 900 KiB, degrade instead of failing — resize
  PNG/JPEG images to a 2000px longest edge (nearest-neighbor, jpeg-js +
  pngjs), drop history pairs from the front, drop the largest images,
  truncate the largest tool results, truncate current content, then hard
  fail. Pure function: never mutates the caller's body, safe across
  endpoint-fallback and integrity-recovery re-sends.

Tests: tests/unit/kiro-schema-normalization.test.js,
tests/unit/kiro-payload-degradation.test.js (20 cases, all green).
No-regression list identical to clean master (88 pre-existing
environmental failures, unchanged).


